:"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A relation links a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"source","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" entity to one or more "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"target","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" entities: a unit likes another,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a turret is aimed at a ship, a part is a child of its parent ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Declare a relation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a type that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Relation"},{"type":"text","text":", then link entities with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/relate(_:_:to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Likes: Relation {}","","var world = World()","let alice = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Alice\"))","let bob = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Bob\"))","world.relate(alice, Likes(), to: bob)","","print(world.targets(Likes.self, of: alice) == [bob])","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","print(world.sources(Likes.self, of: bob) == [alice])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The world stores each link as a pair of a target and a value of the relation, so a relation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can carry data about the link:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Owes: Relation { var amount: Int }","","var world = World()","let alice = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Alice\"))","let bob = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Bob\"))","world.relate(alice, Owes(amount: 20), to: bob)","","if let debt = world[Targets<Owes>.self, of: alice][bob] {","    print(debt.amount)","    \/\/ Prints \"20\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Querying-Relations","text":"Querying Relations","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A source holds its pairs of a relation in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets"},{"text":" component, so you can read and filter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it like any other component. The world also keeps an index of each target’s sources, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"filtering a query with ","type":"text"},{"code":".related(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" visits only the entities related to that target:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let alice = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Alice\"))","let bob = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Bob\"))","let carol = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Carol\"))","world.relate(alice, Likes(), to: bob)","world.relate(carol, Likes(), to: bob)","","let fans = world.query(Name.self).related(Likes.self, to: bob).map { $0.1.value }","print(fans.sorted())","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Alice\", \"Carol\"]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Customizing-a-Relation","text":"Customizing a Relation","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default a source can relate to any number of targets, and despawning a target removes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its pairs from the sources. Implement ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation\/isExclusive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation\/onTargetDespawn","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to change that.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From"},{"kind":"relationships","identifiers